#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105568 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0995bfd4-20b1-5f12-9d1d-fcb180a6291e" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the One-Sided Limits of a Piecewise Function when the Limits Coincide"}] :question/id #uuid "62d73be9-5f67-5f44-a45a-f5c25a4dfe27" :question/math-academy-id "e-64" :question/problem "Find the left- and right-sided limits at $x=1$ of the piecewise function $f(x)$ defined by\n${6e^{x - 1}\\begin{vmatrix}forx < 1 \\\\ x^{2} + 2x + 3\\end{vmatrix}forx > 1$." :question/worked-solution "Approaching from the left, we have $x<1$, so we use the expression\n\n$$\nf(x) = 6e^{x-1}\n$$\n\nWe get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nlim_(x → 1^{-})f(x) &= lim_(x → 1^{-})6e^{x - 1} \\\\\n&= 6e^{1 - 1} \\\\\n&= 6e^{0} \\\\\n&= 6\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApproaching from the right, we have $x>1$, so we use the expression\n\n$$\nf(x) = x^2+2x+3\n$$\n\nWe get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nlim_(x → 1^{+})f(x) &= lim_(x → 1^{+})x^{2} + 2x + 3 \\\\\n&= 1^{2} + 2(1) + 3 \\\\\n&= 6\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105569 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bdd4a2e4-b0e6-54e8-972c-3dc194ce4ab3" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the One-Sided Limits of a Piecewise Function when the Limits Do Not Coincide"}] :question/id #uuid "e9a033d1-eb3f-5e7e-8237-346b03681499" :question/math-academy-id "e-65" :question/problem "Find the left-sided and right-sided limits at $x=0$ for the function\n$f(x) = {-x^{2} + 3\\begin{vmatrix}forx < 0 \\\\ \\sqrt{x}\\end{vmatrix}forx \\ge 0$." :question/worked-solution "Approaching from the left, we have $x < 0$, so we use the expression\n\n$$\nf(x)=-x^2+3\n$$\n\nWe get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nlim_(x → 0^{-})f(x) &= lim_(x → 0^{-})(-x^{2} + 3) \\\\\n&= - (0)^{2} + 3 \\\\\n&= 3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApproaching from the right, we have $x>0$, so we use the expression\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\sqrt{x}\n$$\n\nWe get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nlim_(x → 0^{+})f(x) &= lim_(x → 0^{+})\\sqrt{x} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{0} \\\\\n&= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105570 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9bc794c7-cd0c-5ebc-aa11-9b82e72905fd" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Limits of Piecewise Functions with a Gap in the Domain"}] :question/id #uuid "7f534444-765b-5c3a-a381-883a48911700" :question/math-academy-id "e-66" :question/problem "Find $\\lim_\\limits{x\\rightarrow 1}g(x)$ for the function given by\n${\\frac{\\sqrt{4x^{2} + 5}}{3x - 7}\\begin{vmatrix}forx \\le 1 \\\\ (x - 2)^{2} - 1\\end{vmatrix}forx \\ge 2$." :question/worked-solution "To compute $\\lim\\limits_{x \\to \\, 1} g(x)$, we must compute the left and right-sided limits separately.\n\nHowever, the right-sided limit $\\lim_\\limits{x\\rightarrow 1^+}g(x)$ does not exist since $g(x)$ is not defined in the interval $x\\in(1,2)$.\n\nConsequently, the overall limit does not exist either:\n\n$$\n\\lim_\\limits{x\\rightarrow 1}g(x) = \\text{DNE}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105571 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4014376-4dae-56f1-b981-b35d3afab874" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for a Constant Such that the Limit of a Piecewise Function Exists"}] :question/id #uuid "baed0974-c209-5e29-99b5-d7f1d55b296d" :question/math-academy-id "e-67" :question/problem "For the piecewise function\n$f(x) = {4x^{3} - 2\\begin{vmatrix}forx < 1 \\\\ 3x + b\\end{vmatrix}forx > 1$,\nit is known that $\\lim_\\limits{x\\rightarrow 1}f(x)$ exists. What is the value of the constant $b$?" :question/worked-solution "In order for $\\lim_\\limits{x\\rightarrow 1}f(x)$ to exist, the left and right-sided limits must both exist and be equal.\n\n- Approaching from the left, we have $x < 1$, so we use the expression $f(x)=4x^3-2$. We get\n$lim_(x → 1^{-})f(x)|= lim_(x → 1^{-})4x^{3} - 2; = 4(1)^{3} - 2; = 2$.\n- Approaching from the right, we have $x>1$, so we use the expression $f(x)= 3x+b$. We get\n$lim_(x → 1^{+})f(x)|= lim_(x → 1^{+})3x + b; = 3(1) + b; = 3 + b$.\n\nFinally, since the left and right-sided limits must be equal, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nlim_(x → 1^{-})f(x) &= lim_(x → 1^{+})f(x) \\\\\n2 &= 3 + b \\\\\nb &= -1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106219 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0995bfd4-20b1-5f12-9d1d-fcb180a6291e" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the One-Sided Limits of a Piecewise Function when the Limits Coincide"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a3c5e59b-bd3a-5df8-a9a6-69f7eb6a518f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "lim_(x → 2^{-})f(x) = 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186103824} {:answer/id #uuid "e4cdf6a5-2131-57ee-b209-3b0a2aa7a93c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "lim_(x → 2^{-})f(x) = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186103825} {:answer/id #uuid "ebcb5e6b-81df-52c2-b346-e325771c7d2b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "lim_(x → 2^{-})f(x) = 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186103826} {:answer/id #uuid "05b9a07f-a3fa-55ef-a70e-9cdfa6980358" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "lim_(x → 2^{-})f(x) =-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186103827} {:answer/id #uuid "18a8a0b5-54a7-50d3-95bd-1a3bb5dc0dcd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "lim_(x → 2^{-})f(x) = 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186103828}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e4cdf6a5-2131-57ee-b209-3b0a2aa7a93c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "lim_(x → 2^{-})f(x) = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186103825} :answer-field/id #uuid "3493c78b-2db6-53a0-a112-4b0ca6e94b0c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186103823}] :question/id #uuid "2f374e70-63fe-5c69-b0b8-cea5fdbc9e65" :question/math-academy-id "q-36702" :question/problem "Find the left-sided limit at $x = 2$ of the piecewise function $f(x)$ defined by\n$f(x) = {x^{2} - x - 2\\begin{vmatrix}forx < 2 \\\\ -x^{2} + 6x - 8\\end{vmatrix}forx \\ge 2$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106221 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bdd4a2e4-b0e6-54e8-972c-3dc194ce4ab3" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the One-Sided Limits of a Piecewise Function when the Limits Do Not Coincide"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85e5efc3-6d95-5a3b-bb0a-fbe1793da354" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "lim_(x → 2^{+})f(x) = 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186103836} {:answer/id #uuid "8bf9b025-ca25-5b26-81b0-acced984a77a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "lim_(x → 2^{+})f(x) =-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186103837} {:answer/id #uuid "9303c483-7bef-56b0-8dbf-598237c3dc1e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "lim_(x → 2^{+})f(x) = 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186103838} {:answer/id #uuid "db759a3b-c380-5027-8d6b-f4402e3808c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "lim_(x → 2^{+})f(x) = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186103839} {:answer/id #uuid "fda1a274-15d1-571f-88c0-477ae2a852c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "lim_(x → 2^{+})f(x) = 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186103840}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9303c483-7bef-56b0-8dbf-598237c3dc1e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "lim_(x → 2^{+})f(x) = 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186103838} :answer-field/id #uuid "2507f0bd-fe50-5029-880d-0c1bd7c8b661" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186103835}] :question/id #uuid "879a03e2-86ea-5ccb-9d0a-3118319f3b24" :question/math-academy-id "q-36707" :question/problem "Find the right-sided limit at $x = 2$ for the function\n$f(x) = {x^{2}\\begin{vmatrix}forx \\le 2 \\\\ x\\end{vmatrix}forx > 2$."}]}
